Find the integer $m \in\{1, 2, \dots, n\}$ such that $\psi_{m}=f(x_{m-1})-f(x_{m})$

is maximized;

Let $f_{1}=f(z_{1}), f_{2}=f(z_{n+1})$ , and $f_{3}=f(2z_{n+1}-z_{1})$

if $f_{3}\geq f_{1}$ or $(f_{1}-2f_{2}+f_{3})(f_{1}-f_{2}-\psi_{m})^{2}\geq \frac{1}{2} \psi_{m}(f_{1}-f_{3})^{2}$

Keep the set $p_{1}, p_{2}, \dots, p_{n}$ unchanged and set $x_{k+1}\leftarrow z_{n+1}$

else

Set $\hat{p}\leftarrow z_{n+1}-z_{1}$ and calculate $\hat{\alpha}$ so that $f(z_{n+1}+\hat{\alpha}\hat{p})$ is minimized;

Set $x_{k+1}\leftarrow z_{n+1}+\alpha\hat{p};$

Remove $p_{m}$ from the set of directions and add $\hat{p}$ to this set;

end (if)

